  "savings": {
    "dollars": "none",
    "engine": "lumen_core::savings (crates/lumen-core/src/savings)",
    "reason": "A saving's dollar value is priced at the model of the turn that read the call's result, over the rounds that followed it, and less the extra round the call cost: the savings engine derives these from a ledger's turns. A corpus run has no turns, so this document gives tokens only.",
    "calibrated": true,
    "calibration_note": "Token figures are Claude's tokens, estimated from the cl100k_base counts Lumen records (OpenAI's tokenizer: Claude's is not available offline), by the calibration of 2026-10-14, measured through Claude Code 2.1.296 against Claude's own usage data on 60 samples of raw file text. Each count is converted by its file's type and the model of the turn that read it, at the median ratio for them, with the smallest to the largest ratio any sample came out at as its band (not the 10th to 90th percentile: the floor is the band's low end, and must hold call by call); a row with no measured model takes the type's ratio over both tokenizers, weighted alike, with a band that spans them. The ratios are of raw file text: an answer Lumen makes from a file (an outline, a slice, a stub), a Read's line numbers and the tool-result wrapper around any answer, a Read's or Lumen's, are in no row. So an answer Lumen made takes the file's median, with the smallest to the largest ratio of any sample the model was sent as its band (of any sample at all where the model is not known). The dollar floor takes the low end of each saving: the file at its smallest ratio less Lumen's answer at its largest."
  },
